-- title:
--   p. 1 — H = H(ℝ): Monod's G and H are G(ℝ) and H(ℝ)
-- statement:
--   Monod's group $G$ (`Gpp`: generated by the homeomorphisms of $\mathbf{P}^1$ piecewise in $\mathrm{PSL}_2(\mathbf{R})$, breakpoints anywhere) equals $G(\mathbf{R})$ (`G ⊤`: breakpoints required in $P_{\mathbf{R}}$), and correspondingly Monod's $H$ (`Hpp`) equals $H(\mathbf{R})$ (`H ⊤`).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** `⊤` is the subring $\mathbf{R}$ of $\mathbf{R}$. The source states $H = H(\mathbf{R})$; the equality $G = G(\mathbf{R})$ it rests on is included.
-- source:
--   Monod, N., Groups of piecewise projective homeomorphisms, Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA 110 (2013) 4524–4527, https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1218426110 (arXiv:1209.5229v2, whose page numbers are used), p. 1, after Theorem 2

